# Keep the Composer dist archive to what an application actually needs at
# runtime. Everything below is development tooling: it stays in the Git
# repository and is omitted from `git archive` / `composer require` downloads.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   config/zammad.php  - published at runtime by LaravelServiceProvider
#
# The README links into examples/ and docs/. Those links keep working where the
# README is actually read (GitHub, Packagist); inside an installed vendor/ they
# dangle, which is the trade for not shipping them.
#
# The Symfony Flex recipe under src/Bridge/Symfony/recipe/ is ignored although
# it sits in src/: Flex never reads it from the package, it gets the release
# assets that bin/build-flex-endpoint.php builds from it.
/.github            export-ignore
/bin                export-ignore
/docs               export-ignore
/examples           export-ignore
/test               export-ignore
/src/Bridge/Symfony/recipe export-ignore
/.gitattributes     export-ignore
/.gitignore         export-ignore
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
/Makefile           export-ignore
/SECURITY.asc       export-ignore
/phpcs.xml.dist     export-ignore
/phpstan.neon.dist  export-ignore
/phpunit.xml.dist   export-ignore
